      },
      {
        "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
        "messageId": "0cd1a0df-983a-4118-afc9-4134061c9fbf",
        "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
        "timestamp": 1791655384863,
        "delta": "Deployment #4 in staging failed while building the `worker` service. The error was:\n\n`Building worker failed: npm ERR! Missing script: \"start\"`\n\nnpm reports this when it runs `npm start` in a project whose `package.json` has no `start` script. The failure happened before anything was changed: `web`, `db`, `worker`, and the `pgdata` volume are all marked \"not attempted,\" so staging is still running what deployment #3 applied.\n\nThe config doesn't fully explain the error. `worker` is set to use the image `acme/worker`, with no build source, `startCommand`, or `preDeployCommand`, so I'd expect Ployz to pull the image rather than run an npm build. Deployment #4 also has no recorded builds or upload. Something may have tried to build the worker from source, perhaps a source upload or a path that doesn't match the image setting. I can't see the build log through these tools, so I can't confirm which.\n\nTo fix it, check where the `worker` build comes from. If it should be the `acme/worker` image, the build step is unexpected. If it should be built from source, add a `start` script to that project's `package.json` or set `worker.startCommand`, then deploy again. I haven't changed anything.",
        "content": "Deployment #4 in staging failed while building the `worker` service. The error was:\n\n`Building worker failed: npm ERR! Missing script: \"start\"`\n\nnpm reports this when it runs `npm start` in a project whose `package.json` has no `start` script. The failure happened before anything was changed: `web`, `db`, `worker`, and the `pgdata` volume are all marked \"not attempted,\" so staging is still running what deployment #3 applied.\n\nThe config doesn't fully explain the error. `worker` is set to use the image `acme/worker`, with no build source, `startCommand`, or `preDeployCommand`, so I'd expect Ployz to pull the image rather than run an npm build. Deployment #4 also has no recorded builds or upload. Something may have tried to build the worker from source, perhaps a source upload or a path that doesn't match the image setting. I can't see the build log through these tools, so I can't confirm which.\n\nTo fix it, check where the `worker` build comes from. If it should be the `acme/worker` image, the build step is unexpected. If it should be built from source, add a `start` script to that project's `package.json` or set `worker.startCommand`, then deploy again. I haven't changed anything."
      },
      {
        "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_END",
